  "body": "## What changed\n\nThe Component stack group on the Tool tab of the tool library window now works for a turning tool. Before this change, the group showed only \"A lathe tool's component stack is not resolved yet (#3643).\" PR #4278 added the lathe resolver caller, so the group can now use it.\n\n- The group shows for a lathe-held tool (Turning, Groove, Thread, Form). It uses the same rows, Add component, Remove, Apply stack, Detach and Swap as a spindle tool.\n- An empty stack of a lathe tool offers only the roots that the lathe resolver accepts: a part with a rectangular shank or a round bar shank (`RectShank`, `Cylindrical`, `Weldon`). After the holder, the combo box offers the inserts that fit the holder's seat (`component_fit::compatible_children`).\n- An empty stack of a spindle tool no longer offers a lathe holder (a rectangular shank or a row with a lathe body). The spindle resolver refuses these rows.\n- The values row of a lathe stack shows the gauge length (0, as #4278 decided), \"Inscribed circle (diameter)\", the nose radius and the orientation code. It shows no corner radius, because the lathe resolver does not derive one. A refusal shows by name (\"The stack does not resolve: ...\").\n- Apply stack lands one undoable `SetToolAssembly`, as before.\n- The turning-tool line in the holder area also points to the Component stack.\n- The \"lathe\" test uses the stored record's kind (`tool_body::LATHE_HELD`), the same test as `tool_assembly::derive`.\n\nNo built-in lathe holders or inserts are added. The tools crate has the ISO 5608 and ISO 1832 parsers, but no lathe holder table with sourced seat positions. A user adds lathe holders and inserts to the document from the My library page, from a project file, or with the component editor. The decisions are in `docs/decisions/3898-tool-library-components-3.md`.\n\n## Screenshots\n\nBefore (main): the group refuses a turning tool.\n\n![before](https://raw.githubusercontent.com/qsmits/Camcraft/pr-screenshots/4331/3898-turning-stack-before.png)\n\nAfter: PCLNR2525M12 and CNMG120408 from the document, with the ports, the derived values, and the stack applied.\n\n![after](https://raw.githubusercontent.com/qsmits/Camcraft/pr-screenshots/4331/3898-turning-stack-after.png)\n\nThe screenshots come from a headless render of a test that is not committed.\n\n## Tests\n\nNew file `crates/ui/src/egui_app/tests/tool_library_turning_stack.rs` (the #3648 Done-means item \"assembling a turning tool from linked components\"):\n\n- `a_turning_tool_is_assembled_from_linked_lathe_components_in_one_undo_step`: The user's library holds two PCLNR holders and a CNMG120408 insert. Each \"Add to document\" click is one undo step. The combo box offers only the two lathe holders (not the built-in BT40 ER32 holder in the document), then the insert in seat CSW1. The test clicks both items. The draft shows gauge 0, the IC 12.700 mm, the nose radius 0.800 mm and orientation 2. Apply stack is one undo step and changes the record. Swap is available for the other holder. One undo restores the record exactly, and redo applies the stack again.\n- `a_lathe_stack_the_resolver_refuses_shows_the_refusal_by_name`: A spindle tool's empty stack offers no lathe holder. A groove tool with the same stack shows the resolver's refusal by name. Apply adds no undo step and stores nothing.\n\nThe `#[test]` count of the `camcraft-ui` lib goes from 1766 to 1768.\n\n## Gate results\n\nAll results are on head `d96c8964b`. The runs used macOS, lane 1, with `CAMCRAFT_GATE_JOBS=4` and no sccache.\n\n| Step | Result |\n|---|---|\n| Pinning tests `tool_library_turning_stack::*` (2) | pass |\n| Nearby suites `tool_library_stack`, `tool_library_components`, `tool_library_assembly` (21) | pass |\n| Quick gate `cargo xtask gate quick --base origin/main` (18 steps) | 17 ok. `ui suites: lib` has 1 failure: `setup_wcs_tests::the_combo_lists_the_setups_post_range_by_its_names`. This test is also red on main (#4322) and this PR does not touch it. The other ui lib tests pass: 1759 passed, 1 failed, 8 ignored. |\n| Strict clippy `-p camcraft-ui -p camcraft-app --all-targets -- -D warnings` (clean target) | clean |\n| Light lane `cargo xtask gate light` (6 steps) | 6 ok |\n| Example catalog suites | not run. No post and no toolpath changed. |\n\n## Not exercised\n\n- A lathe holder with a lathe body from the user library: the library refuses rows with a lathe body (#3645). A holder from the library builds the record and no holder body. A holder with a body comes from a project file (pinned on the app side by `lathe_stack.rs`).\n- MCP tools for the component commands are #3647 (PR #4268).\n\n## Done-means check\n\n- #3898: \"a user edits a user holder and a component assembly in the window, with undo, and the Done means list of #3648 is met\". User holders and spindle assemblies merged in #4271 and #4280. This PR adds the turning assembly.\n- #3648: filtering (#4271), assembling a turning tool from linked components (this PR), live update across two tools (#4271), sync from the user library (#4271), undo and redo (all). The UI layout and behaviour tests stay green. The test count does not go down.\n\nChangelog: The tool library window builds a turning tool from linked components: the Component stack offers lathe holders and the inserts that fit them, shows the nose radius, orientation and inscribed circle, and Apply stack is one undo step.\n\nEffort: high\n\nFixes #3898\nFixes #3648\n\n🤖 Generated with [Claude Code](https://claude.com/claude-code)\n",
